From 40f4ec94c3efb56a91f5ad8f2189e407926465fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:47:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban queue reason: comment a new wait reason only
 once it has held 120 s

#2359 stopped volatile-only flaps from commenting, but replaying the real 11-13
flood (197 stored worker_queue_reason payloads of t_01a1d5386cb55abf and
t_01a1d54acc8c8e54, each fed at its recorded time and re-sent every 10 s like
the Board's reserve replies) through it still wrote 42 and 16 worker-placement
comments, 14 and 8 in the worst 10 minutes. They all came from meaning changes
that revert within about a minute: every candidate briefly ineligible
(reserved <-> mixed/admission_limits), a worker draining for its own core update,
a 41 s board_error blip, held on/off.

Fix (hermes_cli/kanban_queue_reason.py):
- Events are unchanged: every meaning change still appends its
  worker_queue_reason event at once, so pickup-stall sightings
  (kanban_pickup_stall._seen_unpinned_here_ms) and latest() stay exact.
- A new meaning is commented only on the first observation at least
  HOLD_MS = 120_000 after the change whose meaning still equals it (describe()
  of that observation). One that reverts or changes again first writes no
  comment; the hold restarts at the newer meaning. A meaning equal to the last
  commented one is no change.
- The hold check also runs on repeat observations (same signature as the
  newest), since the Board's ~10 s repeats are what confirm a hold.
- Still commented at once: the card's first observation, a return to origin
  and a new run (lifecycle run_count changes).
- The volatile refresh rule is kept (one comment per REFRESH_MS for a
  different volatile picture, counted from the last comment), only while the
  meaning equals the commented one.
- The last commented observation, its time and the start of the current
  meaning live in an origin-local table kanban_queue_commented (like
  kanban_queue_latest): a hold is confirmed by a repeat, which is no event.
  Without a row (a card queued before this change) the last event counts as
  commented, as every meaning change then was.

Proof:
- New tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_queue_reason_hold.py with the fixture
  tests/hermes_cli/fixtures/queue-reason-flood-2026-11-13.json. RED on main
  (42 and 16 comments, worst 10 min 14 and 8) and GREEN with the fix (6 and 6
  comments, worst 10 min 2 and 3; acceptance <= 8 and <= 3) on Python 3.11.18
  and 3.14.9. It also pins: a persisting structural change is commented within
  HOLD_MS plus one reply, a revert writes events but no comment, a second
  change restarts the hold, origin and new-run comments are immediate, and a
  sustained Board outage and its recovery are each commented once held.
- The flap tests that pinned immediate comments for meaning changes now
  confirm the hold with one repeat; the 20-minute flap budget test is unchanged
  and green. Tests in other suites that pin which observations are commented
  (not when) run with HOLD_MS=0 via the no_comment_hold fixture.
- The 29 suites importing kanban_queue_reason/repin notice plus all
  pickup-stall suites: 687 passed.

Card: t_01a1d61f47e3f1a0
